## Permission matrix

| Role | Read | Create | Modify | Approve | Close |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| | | | | | |

Rules, inherited from the reference architecture and non-negotiable:

- **Role comes from the authenticated session only** — never from client input, a header, or a request body.
- **Reads default to authenticated staff; writes are allow-listed per role.**
- **Every write names an approver role.** Nothing writes because it seemed reasonable at runtime.
- At least one role should be read-only, and it should be the one that audits.

